### Exercise 9 — Authorization
#
# Run these with the VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client, already recommended
# for this project): click "Send Request" above any request below. No shell needed — works
# the same on Windows, macOS, and Linux.
#
# The response pane shows the HTTP status line at the top — that's what each step checks.
#
# The action requests CHAIN off request 3: send top to bottom to pick an eligible travel,
# then the viewer/reviewer requests reuse its ID automatically — no hardcoded UUIDs.
#
# `cds watch` must be running with Exercise 9's @restrict rules and mocked users.
# Match @acceptFrom to acceptTravel's @from annotation: P for the optional InReview flow
# from Exercise 4, or O if you kept the basic Open -> Accepted flow.
# If request 3 returns an empty value array, create an Open travel using ex3.http. For the
# InReview flow, run ex5.http to create and submit a travel with a booking before retrying.

@host = http://localhost:4004
@acceptFrom = P

### 1) Anonymous read — rejected (expect HTTP 401)
# No Authorization header = anonymous.
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels?$top=1

### 2) Authenticated viewer (no reviewer role) can read (expect HTTP 200)
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels?$top=1
Authorization: Basic viewer:

### 3) Find a travel in the configured acceptance state — SEND BEFORE 4 & 5
# alice (admin) is used just to look it up.
# @name eligibleTravel
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels?$select=ID,description,status_code&$filter=status_code eq '{{acceptFrom}}'&$top=1
Authorization: Basic alice:

### 4) viewer cannot accept (expect HTTP 403)
POST {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels({{eligibleTravel.response.body.$.value[0].ID}})/TravelService.acceptTravel
Authorization: Basic viewer:
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 5) rachel (reviewer) CAN accept (expect HTTP 204)
POST {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels({{eligibleTravel.response.body.$.value[0].ID}})/TravelService.acceptTravel
Authorization: Basic rachel:
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 6) alice (admin) can do everything (expect HTTP 200)
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels?$top=1
Authorization: Basic alice:

### 7) Confirm the reviewer persisted Accepted (expect "status_code":"A")
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels({{eligibleTravel.response.body.$.value[0].ID}})?$select=description,status_code
Authorization: Basic alice:
